   "text": "I read the molecule as a cyclic peptide, built residue by residue from the N-terminus.\n\n**Sequence and ring**\n- N-terminus: hexanoyl\u2013Arg, with a free guanidine side chain.\n- Ring: Pen\u2013Asn\u2013Thr\u2013(7-methyl)Trp\u2013Lys(Ac)\u2013Pen, closed by an S\u2013S bridge between two penicillamine residues (each carrying a C(CH3)2\u2013S group).\n- Tail after the ring: Tyr with an O-CH2CH2NH2 ether, then 2-naphthylalanine, then 4-aminotetrahydropyran-4-carboxylic acid, then Glu (free acid), then Asn, then \u03b1-methyl-Phe as the C-terminal primary amide.\n\n**Stereochemistry**\n- I took the drawn wedges and hashes at each \u03b1-carbon and assigned them from the geometry.\n- Tyr, 2-Nal, Thr (2S,3R) and \u03b1-methyl-Phe come out as L (S).\n- Pen1 (next to the Arg) comes out as D, and Pen2 as L.\n- Arg, Asn, Trp, Lys, Glu and the second Asn are assumed L by default.\n- The Pen1 assignment depends on reading its wedge bond to NH correctly, so that is the least certain stereocentre.\n- The tetrahydropyran carbon is not a stereocentre.\n\nI wrote the SMILES by hand and checked the ring closures and stereo tags for each residue. I did not run it through a parser.\n\nSMILES: CCCCCC(=O)N[C@@H](CCCNC(N)=N)C(=O)N[C@@H]1C(C)(C)SSC(C)(C)[C@@H](C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2ccc(OCCN)cc2)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2ccc3ccccc3c2)C(=O)NC2(CCOCC2)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCC(=O)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)N[C@@](C)(Cc2ccccc2)C(N)=O)NC(=O)[C@H](CCCCNC(C)=O)NC(=O)[C@H](Cc2c[nH]c3c(C)cccc23)NC(=O)[C@H]([C@@H](C)O)NC(=O)[C@H](CC(N)=O)NC1=O"
